look, you're too sturdy.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.180
- No, the little one.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.590
My wife and I are both from the Midwest

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.330
and we're like bigger people.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.070
- Yeah.
- And that little one, man.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.600
It's one thing where
I'm just picking her up

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.500
and then moving her here.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.790
That's one thing.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.770
We went to Yosemite.
- Oh no.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.620
- We went hiking, and I
was like, oh, it's fine.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.131
She can walk uphill.

00:00:24.131 --> 00:00:26.160
And then you realize it's
like a three mile uphill walk.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:26.993
There it is.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:27.908
That's me in front of the--

00:00:27.908 --> 00:00:28.741
- [Kelly] It's beautiful
though, I love Yosemite.

00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:30.060
- I love it, it's amazing.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.380
The majesty of the redwoods.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.730
10 out 10 recommend.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.056
Unless you have a thick baby.

00:00:36.056 --> 00:00:36.960
(audience laughs)

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.100
If you have a thick baby

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.430
you're gonna end up
carrying that thing uphill

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.710
until your arms just start giving out

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.320
and then you pass it on to your wife.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.300
Not it, her, I love you.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.133
I love you.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.590
- It feels like an it,
when it's that heavy.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.600
- It just feels like a sack of potatoes.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.470
- They go dead weight on you.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.303
- They go dead weight.

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:58.440
And so you end up just trading her off

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.700
until three days later

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.500
you go to pick something
up and you can't move

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.320
because your body's so jacked
from carrying a thickie.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.580
- Yes, I have a thickie, yes.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.450
I understand this.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.430
What I do is the piggyback ride.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:09.450
- [Ike] Yes, that's good.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.160
- That's easier for me cuz it's just

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.951
like a backpack with stones in it

00:01:12.951 --> 00:01:16.056
but the problem is then
they start choking you.

00:01:16.056 --> 00:01:16.889
- Yes!

00:01:16.889 --> 00:01:17.790
- 'Cause they get lazy and they choke you

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.050
and I'm like, I need air.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:19.883
- I know.

00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:21.270
I'm always worried that I'm gonna have

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.740
the world's most embarrassing death

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.240
where I'm just slowly asphyxiated

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.893
by my child on my shoulders.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:27.660
It's a real problem, people.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.493
- They're amazing.

00:01:28.493 --> 00:01:30.270
I'm like, I'm not a jungle gym.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.130
- No, we have one at Mindy's house.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:32.963
We'll go there.

00:01:32.963 --> 00:01:34.200
We don't have one at our
house, but Mindy house.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.040
- We have a Capri Sun.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:35.873
- Yes.

00:01:35.873 --> 00:01:37.650
- Well there are a bunch of
talented people in this movie.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.723
So who would you still like to work with?

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.410
- I've been so lucky to work with such

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:47.040
great comedic actors and
drama actors and performers.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.560
I'm kind of looking for the next thing.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.823
And I kind of am looking to
do a collab with Ina Garten.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:55.860
The Barefoot Contessa.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.673
- The Barefoot Contessa.
- That's her right there.

00:01:57.673 --> 00:01:58.680
- [Kelly] I was like, who?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.940
And then I just got it.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.650
- I'm obsessed with her.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.150
- I love you.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.530
- I watch her videos

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.950
and she makes chicken for
her sweet husband, Jeffrey.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.230
And I'm like, this is what I want.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.810
I want to be working with this person.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.520
- This is on your vision board.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.220
- Only her, my vision board
is just one big picture of

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.320
the Barefoot Contessa.

00:02:20.318 --> 00:02:22.980
Obviously we could cook things together,

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.990
but we could solve mysteries together.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.730
We could do a sitcom together.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.460
I just want to be in the
barefoot contessa business.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.510
- I like that.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.920
Solving crime while cooking.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.753
- While cooking.

00:02:33.613 --> 00:02:35.580
A cooking mystery show!

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.840
How good is that?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.002
Thank you.

00:02:38.002 --> 00:02:40.230
- Doesn't everyone wanna dive in this hit?

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.060
- The show's called Dive In.
- Dive in.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.060
- Because it could work on both levels.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.050
- So we were talking about high school.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.000
So in high school did you
ever get caught doing anything

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.833
that you shouldn't?

00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:50.130
I feel like you were maybe a prankster.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.463
- I was a bit of a prankster.
- Okay, that's not shocking.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.310
- I remember for our prom
one year I was like, guys

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.690
I figured out a full proof plan.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.959
I'm gonna get the alcohol.

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:00.240
- Oh my God.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.050
- So I placed this big
order at a liquor store

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.360
and I just used my grandfather's name.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.940
'Cause he passed away.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:09.960
He wasn't gonna use it.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.370
- So he wasn't coming to get any liquor.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.420
- He was not gonna come to claim.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.970
He passed away 10 years before that.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:15.803
And so I went there

00:03:15.803 --> 00:03:17.730
and I found someone to
go in and buy it for us.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.220
And then a month later my dad was like,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.920
hey, I ran into my friend,
Fred who owns the liquor store.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.670
And he said, my dad came in
and ordered a bunch of Zima

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.560
which is funny because my dad

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.370
didn't like Zima and he died in 1986.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.598
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:03:32.598 --> 00:03:34.260
- I got in a little bit
of trouble for that one.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.330
- You live in too small of a town.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.163
- Chicago?

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.592
- Or your family frequents
the liquor store.

00:03:40.592 --> 00:03:42.840
(laughs)

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.250
- A fog is lifting.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.540
- I was like, wait.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.340
- My dad's like I was at
the liquor store again

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.510
this morning.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.660
- I was saying hi to
everyone I know there.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.640
